# `CompletableFuture` — composable async

## Plain `Future.get()` blocks

```java
User u   = fetchUser(id).get();     // block
Orders o = fetchOrders(u).get();     // block again — serialized!
```

## Describe the next step, don't wait

```java
CompletableFuture<Price> result = fetchUser(id)
    .thenCompose(u -> fetchOrders(u))   // chain async step  (like flatMap)
    .thenApply(o -> price(o));          // transform value   (like map)
```

- **`thenApply`** transform · **`thenCompose`** chain async · **`thenAccept`/`thenRun`** consume/act, no value

## Combine independent futures

```java
w.thenCombine(e, (weather, events) -> buildPage(weather, events));
```

`allOf` / `anyOf` fan out to many — "do these at once, then continue."

## Failure travels the chain

```java
fetchUser(id).thenApply(this::render)
    .exceptionally(ex -> fallbackPage(ex));   // a catch for the pipeline
```

**Now:** use it to *fan out & combine*; use plain blocking on virtual threads when sequential.
